                            "Type": "slider_int",
                            "Default": 2,
                            "Description": "How may tiers of difficulty an enemy can be removed from its randomized counterpart. Tiers:\nTier 1 (Low): Basic monsters\nTier 2 (Mid): Level 2-4 Classed NPCs\nTier 3 (High): Midgame monsters, specialized NPCs like Anders\nTier 4 (Ultra): Advanced monsters like Gish'ra, beginner bosses\nTier 5 (Epic): Advanced NPCs and Midgame bosses\nTier 6 (Legendary): Endgame boss NPCs and exceptionally powerful monsters.\nTier 7 (Mythical): Ansur, Netherbrain, and beings comparable to the strongest in the vanilla game\nTier 8 (Divine): Demigods, Tarrasque, creatures adapted from tabletop D&D5e beyond the experience of vanilla BG3\nTier 9 (Avatar): Challenge Rating 30 avatars of true deities, the upper ceiling of D&D5e material.",
